  "notes": "The linear trend is recovered exactly by the centred moving average (the weights are symmetric), so the seasonal indices are exactly [0, 2, 0, -2] and the residuals are 0; rows 0 and 1 have no full window, so trend and residual are NULL (the check pins the first five rows of the 24). ACF/PACF, the drift forecast (slope (v23-v0)/23, sigma from the one-step residuals, z = 1.959963984540054) and the ADF regression (constant plus one lagged difference, normal-approximation p-value) are computed independently in Python."
